{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536883-multiple-rolls-for-magic","id":1536883,"title":"Multiple rolls for magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-07T00:54:56-07:00","id":1536883,"title":"Multiple rolls for magic","content":"Its not really clear in M20 when rerolling a failed spell and adding the +1 difficulty do you start form scratch or do the successes from the former rolls add up.<br /> How do you judge that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T01:23:58-07:00","id":1536884,"title":"","content":"A failed roll didn't have any successes to start with. If you got less successes than you would have liked, and want to try again immediate, all the successes you rolled went into your partially successful spell, no your attempt to try again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T12:25:22-07:00","id":1536896,"title":"","content":"The rule for rolling again with a +1 dif is for ritual casting. In those cases yes, you keep the successes you already had, but failure here means a complete lack of successes on a roll for a spell you were casting as ritual anyway.<br /> <br /> If you're making on spot castings of a single roll, then it is as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, but then the ST may choose to let you roll at normal difficulty, their call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T12:32:43-07:00","id":1536898,"title":"","content":"Trying again at a +1 difficulty is a general rule too, not just one magic, if people are looking for the rules outside of the specifics of complications of ritual casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T13:15:52-07:00","id":1536900,"title":"","content":"im mostly asking about this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Picking Up Where You Left Off<br /> After casting an imperfect Effect or falling short of her initial plans, a mage can pick up where she left off by making another roll at +1 to the original difficulty. In story terms, she grits her teeth, regroups, and gives it the old (wizard) college try once again. For situations in which you try again due to a failed roll \u2013 or try again and fail the roll \u2013 check out the Failed Rolls entry below. In other cases, an extended roll might be in order\u2026 and for those situations, again see the Rituals, Rolls, and Extended Successes entry below.&quot; page 537-538 M20<br /> <br /> Also the deegrees of success table has:<br /> <br /> &quot;Total Failure: No successes. Effect falls short. Mage can try again at +1 difficulty.&quot;<br /> &quot;Partial Success: Player scores roughly half of the Suggested Successes, giving imperfect results. Mage can keep<br /> going, at +1 difficulty&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 06-07-2024, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T13:35:07-07:00","id":1537113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536883-multiple-rolls-for-magic?p=1536898#post1536898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying again at a +1 difficulty is a general rule too, not just one magic, if people are looking for the rules outside of the specifics of complications of ritual casting.</div> </div> </div> </div> I know, but since it is also optional (not as in optional rule, but as in not every roll needing to be under this), there's always the option of just not applying it for most magic roll.<br /> <br /> My experience is that it is rarely interesting to apply to single roll magic, but YMMV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536883-multiple-rolls-for-magic?p=1536900#post1536900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">im mostly asking about this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Picking Up Where You Left Off<br /> After casting an imperfect Effect or falling short of her initial plans, a mage can pick up where she left off by making another roll at +1 to the original difficulty. In story terms, she grits her teeth, regroups, and gives it the old (wizard) college try once again. For situations in which you try again due to a failed roll \u2013 or try again and fail the roll \u2013 check out the Failed Rolls entry below. In other cases, an extended roll might be in order\u2026 and for those situations, again see the Rituals, Rolls, and Extended Successes entry below.&quot; page 537-538 M20<br /> <br /> Also the deegrees of success table has:<br /> <br /> &quot;Total Failure: No successes. Effect falls short. Mage can try again at +1 difficulty.&quot;<br /> &quot;Partial Success: Player scores roughly half of the Suggested Successes, giving imperfect results. Mage can keep<br /> going, at +1 difficulty&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>They're the distinct situations we're talking about.<br /> <br /> You're only ritual casting if you decided to ritual cast from the beginning. In this case, partial successes carry over until the ritual ends (successfully or not) or botches.<br /> <br /> If you tried to make a simple one-roll casting, then a partial success generates a partial result and you need a new casting from scratch if you want a complete result (with or without +1 dif depending on ST's judgement).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T23:08:35-07:00","id":1537133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536883-multiple-rolls-for-magic?p=1537113#post1537113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> They're the distinct situations we're talking about.<br /> <br /> You're only ritual casting if you decided to ritual cast from the beginning. In this case, partial successes carry over until the ritual ends (successfully or not) or botches.<br /> <br /> If you tried to make a simple one-roll casting, then a partial success generates a partial result and you need a new casting from scratch if you want a complete result (with or without +1 dif depending on ST's judgement).</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure?<br /> The deegrees of success table is for general magic casting not just rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T07:07:57-07:00","id":1537149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536883-multiple-rolls-for-magic?p=1537133#post1537133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure?<br /> The deegrees of success table is for general magic casting not just rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no rule whatsoever in the entire book about carrying successes from an Instant Action to another just because you didn't got enough in the first time, so yeah, I'm pretty sure about that.<br /> <br /> You're trying to derive a rule from a table meant for another purpose. It already has all you need to determine the effect of a partial success, but as you said yourself, it has to account for both types of casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T09:10:22-07:00","id":1537155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536883-multiple-rolls-for-magic?p=1537149#post1537149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no rule whatsoever in the entire book about carrying successes from an Instant Action to another just because you didn't got enough in the first time, so yeah, I'm pretty sure about that.<br /> <br /> You're trying to derive a rule from a table meant for another purpose. It already has all you need to determine the effect of a partial success, but as you said yourself, it has to account for both types of casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cited it to you<br /> <br /> &quot;Partial Success: Player scores roughly half of the Suggested Successes, giving imperfect results. Mage can keep going, at +1 difficulty&quot;<br /> <br /> The keep on going part is what makes me wonder. If its not about that then why dthe wording of partial success is different than in total faliure?<br /> <br /> Extended rolls that are not rituals seem to be a bigger things in 2e and revisited but im still uncertain.I mostly agree with you but i feel no one is referencing the things i quoted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T16:29:07-07:00","id":1537176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536883-multiple-rolls-for-magic?p=1537155#post1537155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I cited it to you<br /> <br /> &quot;Partial Success: Player scores roughly half of the Suggested Successes, giving imperfect results. Mage can keep going, at +1 difficulty&quot;<br /> <br /> The keep on going part is what makes me wonder. If its not about that then why dthe wording of partial success is different than in total faliure?<br /> <br /> Extended rolls that are not rituals seem to be a bigger things in 2e and revisited but im still uncertain.I mostly agree with you but i feel no one is referencing the things i quoted.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're quoting from a table that refers to magic rolls from both types. So the table has references for both types. It doesn't mean every reference in the table applies to both, but the opposite, it'll have references relevant to either.<br /> <br /> That quote is exactly what I meant by you trying to derive a rule from a table. It is there because people working a ritual will look at the same table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T23:23:39-07:00","id":1537194,"title":"","content":"Oh i see. That is a valid way to look at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T13:27:01-07:00","id":1537582,"title":"","content":"With all respect meant. I believe Monteparnas is just simply wrong about this. They can play it however they like, but this isn't how it is intended to function.<br /> <br /> There are two types of casting, Standard casting and Ritual casting<br /> <br /> In standard casting, you typically decide how many successes are required by considering how impressive the feat is. Most effects will be around the 3 successes area of impressive, but not always. You can also do this using the divided successes rule to consider how many successes you need in order to do all the things you intend. This number becomes your Target successes<br /> <br /> Each roll has 3 potential outcomes:<br /> 1) You roll enough successes, if you do this then your effect goes off, any excess successes can be used to augment the effect in some way, make it last longer, deal more damage, or become more impressive at the ST's discretion.<br /> 2) You do not roll enough successes (any number below the target, including 0) You now have a choice, you can roll again at +1 difficulty to accumulate more successes (This is what is meant by pick up where they left off), or you can stop and accept a partial cast (which is either determined by dividing the successes you did accumulate, or by using the table you quoted).<br /> 3) You botch, no further attempts may be tried, enjoy your paradox.<br /> <br /> Rituals change this in the following ways:<br /> First, you only get an increase to difficulty on a failed roll (that is rolling no successes)<br /> Second, you can save your spell from your first botch, but you lose a successes and increase the difficulty, botching a second time destroys the effect and leads to ever more paradox<br /> Third, you can cast in tandem with other mages.<br /> <br /> A note on paradox: For vulgar effects you gain a point of paradox whether or not you succeed or fail the roll (This is specifically stated in Revised, and it exists as well in M20, though it isn't well communicated). One can interpret that on each failed roll in a standard cast, that is a point of paradox crewed regardless of whether or not you decide to pick up where you left off and roll again. Rituals on the other hand only give paradox per roll upon a botch. This means standard casting as an extended roll is actually far more paradox prone then ritual casting, which I also believe is the intent.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I hope that clears up a few things, or at least inspires you to run it in a way which best reflects the areas you wish to emphasise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 06-22-2024, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T15:47:59-07:00","id":1537586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536883-multiple-rolls-for-magic?p=1537582#post1537582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all respect meant. I believe Monteparnas is just simply wrong about this. They can play it however they like, but this isn't how it is intended to function.<br /> <br /> There are two types of casting, Standard casting and Ritual casting<br /> <br /> In standard casting, you typically decide how many successes are required by considering how impressive the feat is. Most effects will be around the 3 successes area of impressive, but not always. You can also do this using the divided successes rule to consider how many successes you need in order to do all the things you intend. This number becomes your Target successes<br /> <br /> Each roll has 3 potential outcomes:<br /> 1) You roll enough successes, if you do this then your effect goes off, any excess effects can be used to augment the effect in some way, make it last longer, deal more damage, or become more impressive at the ST's discretion.<br /> 2) You do not roll enough successes (any number below the target, including 0) You now have a choice, you can roll again at +1 difficulty to accumulate more successes (This is what is meant by pick up where they left off), or you can stop and accept a partial cast (which is either determined by dividing the successes you did accumulate, or by using the table you quoted).<br /> 3) You botch, no further attempts may be tried, enjoy your paradox.<br /> <br /> Rituals change this in the following ways:<br /> First, you only get an increase to difficulty on a failed roll (that is rolling no successes)<br /> Second, you can save your spell from your first botch, but you lose a successes and increase the difficulty, botching a second time destroys the effect and leads to ever more paradox<br /> Third, you can cast in tandem with other mages.<br /> <br /> A note on paradox: For vulgar effects you gain a point of paradox whether or not you succeed or fail the roll (This is specifically stated in Revised, and it exists as well in M20, though it isn't well communicated). One can interpret that on each failed roll in a standard cast, that is a point of paradox crewed regardless of whether or not you decide to pick up where you left off and roll again. Rituals on the other hand only give paradox per roll upon a botch. This means standard casting as an extended roll is actually far more paradox prone then ritual casting, which I also believe is the intent.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I hope that clears up a few things, or at least inspires you to run it in a way which best reflects the areas you wish to emphasise.Speak</div> </div> </div> </div>With all respect meant...<br /> <br /> I will accept your interpretation and integrate it on my own ongoing Mage chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}